meta {
  name: Symbol Requests
  seq: 13
}

docs {
  User-facing "request a symbol be added" flow, surfaced from Paper Trading's
  "unknown or inactive symbol" rejection:
  - POST /v1/symbol-requests
  - GET  /v1/symbol-requests

  Admin review (accept/reject/list) lives in the Admin folder's
  symbol-requests-*.bru files — accepting a request doesn't resolve it by
  itself; resolution happens automatically the moment a matching instrument
  is created (Admin > POST Create Instrument), which is exercised there too.

  **Run this folder before Admin/login.bru in the same invocation** — that
  request overwrites {{token}} with the admin's token, so the regular-user
  requests here (which use {{token}}) must run first:
    npx @usebruno/cli run "Auth/login.bru" -r "Symbol Requests" -r "Admin/login.bru" -r "Admin" --env local

  **Key facts:**
  - `market_profile_code` must reference an existing, active market profile
    (e.g. `indian_equity`) — reason is required.
  - A user can only have one active (pending/accepted) request per
    profile+symbol — a second attempt 409s (see duplicate-rejected.bru).
  - Status: pending -> accepted -> resolved (auto), or pending/accepted ->
    rejected.
}
